        "title": "Drinking Water Treatment",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Drinking water treatment is a **pipeline of composable unit operations** — each stage has defined inputs, outputs, and a removal transfer function. The composition of stages is the same architecture as an ETL pipeline, a compiler pass chain, or a signal processing cascade: raw input enters, each stage transforms it, and the cumulative effect of the chain achieves the target output spec. Design is driven by source water quality and regulatory requirements."
